WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.646
[Katherine Dunham] For one thing, I was
seeking to maintain an academic level.

2
00:00:10.646 --> 00:00:17.727
I knew that dance was something I had
to do. I had no choice in it at all.

3
00:00:17.727 --> 00:00:25.000
And I knew that it was regarded, had a
certain position in the world of art.

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.557
But it had no position whatsoever
in the academic world.

5
00:00:30.557 --> 00:00:38.000
I mean, even sports would have been
considered closer, I think, than dance.

6
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.377
So my problem was to remain an
investigator, an intelligent investigator,

7
00:00:46.377 --> 00:00:55.443
a productive one, in academics, where
certainly anthropology was a new science,

8
00:00:55.443 --> 00:00:59.000
but it was very much respected.

9
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.596
And my problem, my strong
drive at that time,

10
00:01:04.596 --> 00:01:12.803
was to remain in this academic
position that anthropology gave me,

11
00:01:12.803 --> 00:01:23.000
and at the same time, continue with this
strong drive for motion, rhythmic motion.

